  "notes": "County-level breakdown is from the official 'Active Voters by County and Party' PDF (06/08/2026) and reflects ACTIVE voters only; party counts sum exactly to each county total and to the statewide active total of 1,775,519 (verified). Original PDF parties: Republican, Democratic, Unaffiliated, Libertarian, Independent American, Constitution, Green, Forward. 'Other' here aggregates Independent American (76,143), Constitution (6,636), Green (1,054), and Forward (2,243). NOTE: The vote.utah.gov statewide summary page reports a larger total of 2,083,525 because it includes INACTIVE voters in addition to active (e.g., Republican 1,033,712; Democratic 295,737; Unaffiliated 621,928 active+inactive). No county-level active+inactive breakdown is published; this file uses the active-only county source for internal consistency."
